# Build inputs. These generate the HTML that ships; they are not part of the
# site itself and must never be publicly served.
#
# data/ holds tax-rates.json, the source the rate tables and calculators are
# generated FROM. What ships to the browser is js/tax-rates.js, which build.py
# writes from it — serving the JSON too would put two copies of the same
# figures on the site, which is the exact problem this file solved.
build.py
site.json
content/
data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Calculators — switched OFF (site.json -> features.calculators = false).
#
# Nothing links to the tools section any more and build.py no longer writes it,
# but the HTML it wrote on the last build is still committed here and Workers
# Assets would happily keep serving it at the old URLs. Ignoring it takes those
# files out of the deployed output without deleting a line of the source, and
# `_redirects` sends /tools and /tools/* to /resources instead.
#
# To bring the calculators back: set features.calculators to true in site.json,
# run `python build.py`, delete this block and the two /tools rules in
# `_redirects`. The pages regenerate exactly as they were.
tools.html
tools/
js/tax-rates.js
js/sa-tax-core.js
js/income-tax-calculator.js
js/bonus-tax-calculator.js
js/net-to-gross-calculator.js
js/provisional-tax-calculator.js
js/small-business-tax-calculator.js
js/vat-calculator.js
js/cipc-fee-calculator.js
js/sars-penalty-calculator.js
js/employer-cost-calculator.js
